  "description": "Standalone MQTT nodes for FluxFlow over an injected client adapter: a connection handle that owns the client lifecycle (host-driven connect/disconnect), publish (request in, result out) and subscribe (received messages out) nodes that borrow the established adapter, and an MQTT5 request/reply trigger (MqttRequestContext + the transport-neutral RequestReplyCoordinator). One package for the whole MQTT surface — connection, publish, subscribe, and trigger. Broadcast output/error/event ports. No engine required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Mqtt",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-19T14:30:54.493Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "I8QXbOpxIikjUz1+lZ0bmiF+BOF/uMzjvmDUVhvfUYHOLkQalXGV5b4G+XUcdhxwOYgnk9l+tnE+Q4vcO5eLSg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 77293,
  "published": "2026-06-19T14:27:45.92Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt as standalone nodes over the FluxFlow.Nodes kit: the engine and designer dependencies are removed. mqtt.connection becomes a self-contained connection handle (IMqttConnectionHandle) that owns the single client lease, epoch, health monitor, and host-driven ConnectAsync/DisconnectAsync lifecycle, exposing connection health on a broadcast FlowEvent port; the carefully hardened gate/single-flight/lease-ordering/dispose-race concurrency is unchanged. mqtt.publish becomes a FlowNode (MqttPublishRequest in, MqttPublishResult out) and mqtt.subscribe a FlowSource (MqttReceivedMessage out); both borrow the established adapter when connected (subscribe (re)subscribes per connection epoch) and report not-connected on the error port otherwise, never connecting or disposing. NodeAddress is dropped; the connection identity is its ConnectionName. The node registration module, factories, ports, options reader, component types, and design-metadata provider are removed. Contracts, options, topic validation, and diagnostics are preserved. The MQTT request/reply trigger (formerly the separate FluxFlow.Components.Mqtt.RequestReply package) is now folded into this single MQTT package: MqttRequestContext writes the correlated reply to the MQTT5 response topic via a host-supplied IMqttResponsePublisher, driving the transport-neutral RequestReplyCoordinator.",
